---
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import LocationCard from '../../components/LocationCard.astro';
import QuoteCta from '../../components/QuoteCta.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { locations } from '../../data/locations';
import { siteConfig } from '../../data/site';
import { getKeywordTarget } from '../../lib/seo-keywords';

const seo = getKeywordTarget('/locations/');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={seo.primaryKeyword}
  description="Explore valet parking service areas in Philadelphia, Center City, the Main Line, King of Prussia, Bucks County, and South Jersey."
  canonicalPath="/locations/"
  image="/images/valet-hero-philadelphia.webp"
  imageAlt="Uniformed valet attendant working at a Philadelphia curb in direct afternoon light"
  pageType="CollectionPage"
  schema={{
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: siteConfig.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Service areas', item: `${siteConfig.url}/locations/` },
    ],
  }}
>
  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="locations-page-title">
    <div class="panel panel-dark grid text-white lg:grid-cols-[0.94fr_1.06fr]">
      <div class="section-pad flex flex-col justify-center">
        <Breadcrumbs inverse items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Locations' }]} />
        <p class="eyebrow mt-8">Locations hub</p>
        <h1 id="locations-page-title" class="display-title mt-7 max-w-[11ch]">{seo.primaryKeyword}.</h1>
        <p class="body-large mt-7 text-white/66">Compare {seo.supportingKeywords[0]} across dense blocks, private drives, regional venues, garages, and remote lots. {seo.supportingKeywords[1][0].toUpperCase() + seo.supportingKeywords[1].slice(1)} is confirmed from the exact address and operating plan.</p>
        <a href="#location-list" class="button-light mt-8 self-start">Find your area<Arrow direction="down" /></a>
      </div>
      <div class="relative min-h-[34rem] overflow-hidden border-t border-white/12 lg:min-h-[46rem] lg:border-t-0 lg:border-l">
        <img src="/images/valet-hero-philadelphia.webp" alt="Valet service at a Philadelphia curb in direct afternoon light" width="1800" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover" />
        <div class="absolute right-4 bottom-4 left-4 border border-white/20 bg-navy-deep/88 p-5 backdrop-blur-sm sm:left-auto sm:max-w-sm">
          <p class="text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.14em] text-signal uppercase">Coverage check</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/72">Do not see your municipality listed? Share the address and service date. Coverage and travel details are confirmed with each request.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="location-list" class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="location-list-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad">
      <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.75fr] lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Six planning areas</p>
          <h2 id="location-list-title" class="section-title mt-6">Choose the place that best matches the site.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink/64">These pages describe common operating conditions and venue types. Final service availability depends on the address, schedule, and parking plan.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {locations.map((location, index) => <LocationCard location={location} index={index} />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="location-method-title">
    <div class="panel panel-river section-pad">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What location changes</p>
          <h2 id="location-method-title" class="section-title mt-6">Distance is only one part of the map.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-px overflow-hidden border border-navy/15 bg-navy/15 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {[
            ['The handoff', 'Curb width, private drive geometry, loading activity, and pedestrian access define where guests should stop.'],
            ['The storage route', 'A nearby garage, remote lot, field, or street arrangement changes cycle time and staffing.'],
            ['The peak', 'Dinner reservations, ceremony timing, appointments, hotel check-in, and event close all produce different demand curves.'],
            ['The neighborhood', 'Residents, deliveries, transit, bicycles, rideshare vehicles, and venue neighbors belong in the plan.'],
          ].map(([title, body]) => (
            <article class="bg-river p-6 sm:p-8">
              <h3 class="card-title">{title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink/66">{body}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="coverage-review-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad">
      <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.72fr_1.28fr] lg:gap-20">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">How coverage is reviewed</p>
          <h2 id="coverage-review-title" class="section-title mt-6">A city name does not settle the operating question.</h2>
          <p class="mt-6 text-ink/65">The regional pages explain common conditions, but the final answer comes from the property, parking route, schedule, and available crew plan.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rich-copy text-lg text-ink/66">
          <p>Coverage begins with the full service address and preferred guest entrance. Two properties in the same municipality can require completely different plans when one uses a short urban curb and the other uses a private drive with remote parking.</p>
          <p>The first review also needs the date or recurring schedule, expected vehicle volume, property or event type, proposed parking area, and known access constraints. Garage credentials, shared driveways, loading windows, shuttles, surface conditions, and night lighting can all change feasibility and staffing.</p>
          <p>The listed neighborhoods and municipalities are orientation points, not a promise that every address is automatically available. If a place is outside the examples, send the same site facts. Travel, access, permissions, and the operating arrangement can then be evaluated without forcing the property into the wrong regional description.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteCta eyebrow="Outside the listed areas?" title="Send the address. We will start there." body="Coverage, travel, curb conditions, and available parking are confirmed before a service plan is proposed." />
</BaseLayout>
